  "text": "I would be happy to help you make a delicious classic Neapolitan ice cream. Here's a simple recipe you can follow:\n\n1. In a large bowl, mix 2 cups of heavy cream, 1 cup of whole milk, 3/4 cup of sugar, and 1 teaspoon of vanilla extract until the sugar is completely dissolved.\n\n2. The whipped cream should be smooth and creamy, not too runny. Stretch it until it reaches a syrupy consistency, then mix in the soaked gelatin until it is fully dissolved.\n\n3. Once the gelatin is fully dissolved, add the sugar, vanilla extract, and any other flavorings you desire to the whipped cream and mix until everything is well combined.\n\n4. Finally, pour the mixture into a clean, sealed container and refrigerate it for at least 6 hours or overnight.\n\nEnjoy your classic Neapolitan ice cream!",
